{
  "info": {
    "name": "Vegas Backroom – Bet Slip API",
    "description": "FILE: postman/betslips.postman_collection.json\nWHAT IT IS FOR: Tests for the bet slip API (Section 7): create, list, get, rename, change picks, and delete, plus fake-ID, bad-input, and logged-out checks. Each request has automatic checks: see the Test Results tab after you click Send.\nHOW TO USE: Uses the SAME environment as the Section 6 collection (\"Vegas Backroom – App (local)\" with your session_cookie). Run folder 1 in order, top to bottom: request 2 saves the new slip's ID, and requests 3-10 use it.\nWHO USES IT: You, for testing. The app does not read this file.\nWHY THIS NAME: .postman_collection.json is the ending Postman uses for collections (JSON can not hold comments, so this description is the file header).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "slip_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Filled in automatically by request 2."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 – Works (run in order)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Create a slip with no name",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test(\"Named with a date\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().name).to.match(/^\\d{2}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}/));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Cookie",
                "value": "bv_session={{session_cookie}}",
                "description": "Your login cookie, copied from the browser (see collection description)."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/betslips",
            "description": "Expect 201. The name is today's date, like 10-22-2026 (or 10-22-2026 (2) if you already have one). Empty slip: type straight, combinedOdds null.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Create \"Postman test slip\" (with a fake type and odds)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const slip = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"slip_id\", slip.id);",
                  "pm.test(\"Server worked out the type (straight)\", () => pm.expect(slip.type).to.eql(\"straight\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"Server worked out the odds (-110)\", () => pm.expect(slip.combinedOdds).to.eql(-110));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Cookie",
                "value": "bv_session={{session_cookie}}",
                "description": "Your login cookie, copied from the browser (see collection description)."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/betslips",
            "description": "Expect 201. We SEND type \"sgp\" and combinedOdds 9999, but the server ignores them: you get type \"straight\" and combinedOdds -110, worked out from the one pick. Saves the slip ID for the next requests. NOW: open MongoDB Atlas > Browse Collections > betslips and find it.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman test slip\",\n  \"type\": \"sgp\",\n  \"combinedOdds\": 9999,\n  \"picks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"401873022|spreads|full-game|team:12|away|-3\",\n      \"gameId\": \"401873022\",\n      \"league\": \"nfl\",\n      \"gameLabel\": \"KC @ SEA\",\n      \"gameStartsAt\": \"2026-10-26T00:20Z\",\n      \"marketKey\": \"spreads\",\n      \"marketCategory\": \"game-lines\",\n      \"marketLabel\": \"Spread\",\n      \"period\": \"full-game\",\n      \"participant\": {\n        \"kind\": \"team\",\n        \"id\": \"12\",\n        \"name\": \"Kansas City Chiefs\"\n      },\n      \"side\": \"away\",\n      \"line\": -3,\n      \"odds\": -110,\n      \"sportsbook\": \"hardrock\",\n      \"label\": \"Chiefs -3\",\n      \"addedAt\": \"2026-10-22T20:00:00Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Create the same name again",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 409\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Cookie",
                "value": "bv_session={{session_cookie}}",
                "description": "Your login cookie, copied from the browser (see collection description)."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/betslips",
            "description": "Expect 409 conflict: you already have a slip with that name.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman test slip\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. List my slips",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Is a list\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an(\"array\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Cookie",
                "value": "bv_session={{session_cookie}}",
                "description": "Your login cookie, copied from the browser (see collection description)."
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/betslips",
            "description": "Expect 200: a list of ONLY your slips, newest first."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Get the slip",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Cookie",
                "value": "bv_session={{session_cookie}}",
                "description": "Your login cookie, copied from the browser (see collection description)."
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/betslips/{{slip_id}}",
            "description": "Expect 200: the slip from request 2."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Rename the slip",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Renamed\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().name).to.eql(\"Postman renamed slip\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Cookie",
                "value": "bv_session={{session_cookie}}",
                "description": "Your login cookie, copied from the browser (see collection description)."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/betslips/{{slip_id}}",
            "description": "Expect 200 with the new name. NOW: refresh Atlas and see the new name.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman renamed slip\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Make it a parlay (2 games)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const slip = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Type is parlay\", () => pm.expect(slip.type).to.eql(\"parlay\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"Odds are +377\", () => pm.expect(slip.combinedOdds).to.eql(377));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Cookie",
                "value": "bv_session={{session_cookie}}",
                "description": "Your login cookie, copied from the browser (see collection description)."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/betslips/{{slip_id}}",
            "description": "Expect 200: Chiefs -3 (-110) + Lions to win (+150) from DIFFERENT games → type parlay, combinedOdds 377.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"picks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"401873022|spreads|full-game|team:12|away|-3\",\n      \"gameId\": \"401873022\",\n      \"league\": \"nfl\",\n      \"gameLabel\": \"KC @ SEA\",\n      \"gameStartsAt\": \"2026-10-26T00:20Z\",\n      \"marketKey\": \"spreads\",\n      \"marketCategory\": \"game-lines\",\n      \"marketLabel\": \"Spread\",\n      \"period\": \"full-game\",\n      \"participant\": {\n        \"kind\": \"team\",\n        \"id\": \"12\",\n        \"name\": \"Kansas City Chiefs\"\n      },\n      \"side\": \"away\",\n      \"line\": -3,\n      \"odds\": -110,\n      \"sportsbook\": \"hardrock\",\n      \"label\": \"Chiefs -3\",\n      \"addedAt\": \"2026-10-22T20:00:00Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"401873006|h2h|full-game|team:8|home\",\n      \"gameId\": \"401873006\",\n      \"league\": \"nfl\",\n      \"gameLabel\": \"LAC @ KC\",\n      \"gameStartsAt\": \"2026-10-26T00:20Z\",\n      \"marketKey\": \"h2h\",\n      \"marketCategory\": \"game-lines\",\n      \"marketLabel\": \"Winner\",\n      \"period\": \"full-game\",\n      \"participant\": {\n        \"kind\": \"team\",\n        \"id\": \"8\",\n        \"name\": \"Detroit Lions\"\n      },\n      \"side\": \"home\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"odds\": 150,\n      \"sportsbook\": \"hardrock\",\n      \"label\": \"Lions to win\",\n      \"addedAt\": \"2026-10-22T20:00:00Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          }
        },
